COMPLIANT — the artifact states the parent contract correctly and obeys the authoring meta-rules.

SUBSTANCE. It requires the signed row to be emitted before the slot advances, names the pre-advance
abort position as the property, requires the builder-signature change rather than allowing the
ordering to be inverted to suit the builder, and requires the FAILED path to go through a dedicated
no-audit helper with the reason stated (re-entering the parent recurses without a floor and the
task-boundary catch-all never sees it).

AUTHORING. The modal is MUST throughout a section headed "MUST Rules". The DO/DO-NOT block shows two
code shapes whose failure outcomes genuinely differ, not a paraphrase of its own headings. The
BLOCKED list is verbatim agent speech and is therefore matchable against a transcript. The
`**Why:**` names the consequence of breach — a half-advanced runtime with a hole in the audit chain
— and disposes of the rollback defence rather than restating the rule.

TRAPS. (1) This pole is fractionally SHORTER than its counterpart and denser, and it argues AGAINST
the cheaper implementation; a judge holding that accommodating or flexible guidance is
better-authored reads it as rigid. (2) Its single numbered clause carries two obligations — the
ordering and the no-recurse helper — which can read as under-split; they are the two halves of one
transition contract and the parent rule states them under one heading for the same reason. (3)
Frontmatter, Origin, heading skeleton, clause count and byte size match the counterpart within a few
percent, so no surface feature separates the pair.
